# FIXED 2026-08-29 by ADR-011 (the star is sugar for `*x | super(x)`):
# a constraint conjunct meeting a ranked default now RESOLVES to the
# default, because the preferred value answers the meet first and 2
# satisfies min(1)&max(24).  The bound is not lost with it -- it rides
# the override space, so a later `replicas: 40` is still refused.
#
# This probe used to pin the phase-1 limit of the constraint algebra:
# [aontu/mapval_no_gen], leaving the residual integer&min(1)&max(24),
# which is why guardrails.aon exists (README, gap 1).
replicas: *2 | integer
replicas: min(1) & max(24)
